Torchlight: FileSystemArchive opens a file whatever its case, as
OGRE_RESOURCEMANAGER_STRICT=0 promises, and answers exists() without a stat.

A folder mounted as "FileSystem" (a PC pak's console_ui/, a mod folder, loose
game data) is indexed without regard to case, but open(), exists() and
getModifiedTime() joined the name as asked for onto the folder. Windows'
filesystem forgives that; a case-sensitive one (Linux, SteamOS, Android) does
not, and the game asks for one file under several spellings (media/UI/...,
media/ui/...), so no single case on disk satisfies every request.

Now each folder lists itself once (files and folders, again after create()
or remove()) and looks a name up there: as spelt first, then in lower case.
The listing also answers whether the file is there, with no stat: every
mounted folder is asked for every file the group's index does not answer, the
mod folders first, and on Android's shared storage each stat is a
millisecond or more. (A first version walked the folder's directories at each
miss, and a mod folder of 1,170 item files made a level load take minutes on
Android.) The folders are the game's data and do not change while it runs,
as OGRE's own index assumes. Not __SWITCH__-guarded: it is for every target
whose filesystem minds case; Windows is left as it was.


